o the  transportation also transition to trauma  and then transporting the stuff from the  farm to the market and all the things  that need to be done in between in terms  of building a cold chain so that that  that products from a from a farm can be  preserved in cold storage can go and  refrigerated trucks so there's a huge  amount of work with on the supply chain  and each of these means both investment  in money that is a tree infrastructure  also hopefully getting the best use of  new technology available in the world ok  you touched upon the global economic  crisis when we began how do you what  role do you think india has to play in  that i think unfortunately not much  really except making sure they don't  that we don't contribute to it but so  far we haven't the i guess the only  other role that we could play hopefully  is that one one thing that strikes me  for example is that just like United  States peer a federal system and so  there is structure of fiscal federalism  in terms of what the different Indian  states can do  in terms of borrowing and in terms of  the kind of intended nests that they can  get into there's certain disciplines to  do with that and so one of the issues  that is arising in Europe is and they're  having meeting today the the summit  between the Prime Minister's the leaders  of the European countries today and talk  about a fiscal Union and then obviously  what what they want is some kind of  discipline that some central authority  like the European Commission the  European Union will then have over the  different european countries now we have  that in the sense that we are of course  an integrated country and not different  countries but we have a large number of  states like the u.s. does and they all  borrow in the market but we do have  certain rules under which they operate  so that they don't get excessively  indebted I think that maybe as the  European fiscal Union does start  operating if they succeed this evening  and th